 "answer": "Matter 1013-00004 involves IRB in its work product (clinical evidence gap analysis, NCD feasibility assessment, MolDx dossier all discuss IRB approvals). ✓\n\nI'm confident in my final list. Let me provide the answer.\n\nBased on my thorough analysis of the firm's document management system, I've identified the Healthcare & Life Sciences matters that involved informed consent or an IRB.\n\n## Summary\n\nThere are **5** Healthcare & Life Sciences matters that involved informed consent or an IRB:\n\n1. **1013-00004** — Genome Dx Therapeutics (GDT) Medicare coverage & coding strategy for OncoPrecise GXP-47. This Healthcare & Life Sciences matter involved IRB in its clinical evidence analysis (IRB approvals at clinical trial sites, IRB approval requirements for study protocols).\n\n2. **1018-00004** — Penterra Pharmaceuticals / Veridian Health Research Network Master Clinical Trial Agreement (CLARION Phase III trial). This Healthcare & Life Sciences matter involved both IRB (IRB approvals, central IRB reliance, IRB submission strategy) and informed consent (informed consent forms, informed consent procedures, HIPAA research authorizations).\n\n3. **1018-00005** — Penterra Pharmaceuticals sNDA labeling supplement for Velonatib. This Healthcare & Life Sciences matter involved IRB (preparing and submitting IRB/ethics committee applications for clinical trial sites in the pediatric deferral analysis).\n\n4. **1029-00001** — TMRI clinical trial agreement (Cadence-3 trial). This Healthcare & Life Sciences matter involved both IRB (IRB approval, IRB protocol) and informed consent (informed consent procedures, informed consent failures in indemnification analysis).\n\n5. **1037-00002** — Solstice Biomedical FDA regulatory strategy for the Lumina CGM system (LUMINA-US clinical study). This Healthcare & Life Sciences matter involved both IRB (IRB submission strategy, Clearwater IRB) and informed consent (informed consent templates, informed consent documents).\n\n**Qualifying matter IDs: 1013-00004, 1018-00004, 1018-00005, 1029-00001, 1037-00002**\n\nNote: I excluded several matters that mention \"informed consent\" or \"IRB\" but are not Healthcare & Life Sciences matters (e.g., conflict-of-interest waivers in engagement letters, or clinical-trial matters handled by other practice groups such as Capital Markets, IP Litigation, or M&A special committees). I also excluded H&LS matters where the only \"informed consent\" reference was a legal-ethics conflict waiver rather than clinical-trial informed consent.",
